From: WinTone01 <mertbayinma792@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 05:27:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Lazy packet scheduling unless the event loop is wrapped

Paper PR 10172 (via Leaf) hands packets that are not flushed to the
connection's thread with lazyExecute, which does not wake it up. Leaf
keeps it off because ProtocolLib wraps the event loop and lazyExecute on
the cached real loop would bypass it; Shulker turns it on per connection
when the channel still returns the real loop. 40 players + 1500 mobs:
about 40% less CPU time on the Netty threads.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
index 064ef558131eff4547139a3479bd0e50202ee0b3..69496b41c5a8c39ec0836ba90ee30c80b7af9da3 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/Connection.java
@@ -527,7 +527,8 @@ public class Connection extends SimpleChannelInboundHandler<Packet<?>> {
             this.doSendPacket(packet, listener, flush);
         } else {
             // Paper start - optimise packets that are not flushed
-            if (!flush && org.dreeam.leaf.config.modules.network.OptimizeNonFlushPacketSending.enabled) {
+            if (!flush && (org.dreeam.leaf.config.modules.network.OptimizeNonFlushPacketSending.enabled
+                || dev.shulker.server.ShulkerConfig.lazyPacketScheduling && this.channel.eventLoop() == this.eventLoop)) { // Shulker - on unless a plugin wrapped the event loop (ProtocolLib), which lazyExecute would bypass
                 this.eventLoop.lazyExecute(() -> this.doSendPacket(packet, listener, false));
             } else
                 // Paper end - optimise packets that are not flushed
